WEBVTT

00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:15,280
In a call with my doctor this morning she introduced the idea of metronomic chemotherapy,

00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:17,320
that is 10% of the normal strength.

00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:21,520
I searched your site and didn't see a topic mentioned.

00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:26,960
I would assume this would have considerably reduced side effects.

00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:32,880
We have been successful at keeping the prostate toer from spreading for about five years now,

00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:37,880
but we don't seem to be making significant progress at knocking it down.

00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:42,600
I have avoided the toxic and invasive treatments thus far.

00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:49,560
Do you see metronomic chemotherapy as a logical baby step in that direction?

00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:56,120
So yeah, you're just trying to think through your option.

00:00:56,120 --> 00:01:04,680
So number one, metronomic or if you're using insulin to stimulate the uptake of it,

00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:07,400
it's called insulin-potentiated chemotherapy.

00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:11,720
So you're giving a shot of insulin, waiting for a period of time,

00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:14,760
and then doing 10% the dosage of chemotherapy.

00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:22,040
Well that idea first surfaced about 25 years ago.

00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:29,240
It was very exciting because if we could get the cancer cells to uptake the chemotherapy,

00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:35,560
much more efficiently, could we not give a lower dose of chemotherapy?

00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:42,360
Well, it had been proven to be successful, but the problem is it's not always successful

00:01:42,360 --> 00:01:48,440
like anything else. First of all, if chemotherapy isn't going to, if full dose chemotherapy isn't

00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:53,800
going to work for a person, then then low dose chemotherapy isn't going to work for the person.

00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,280
And the truth is, is that full dose chemotherapy only works for a percentage of people.

00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:08,760
So if the full dose is not going to work for you, then the low doses are going to work for you.

00:02:09,720 --> 00:02:15,640
So chemotherapy is a drug that's increasing oxidative stress.

00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:26,040
What's problem is it doesn't work for everybody. So it's then that's the struggle. Now with prostate

00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:36,280
cancer, I'm surprised they're offering that to you because prostate cancer historically doesn't have

00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:44,600
a great success rate with chemotherapy. It's not typically what is even recommended unless

00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:50,840
they have run out of other options. Typically with prostate cancer, they will recommend

00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:56,040
androgen deprivation therapy, which basically shuts down all your testosterone. They'll

00:02:56,040 --> 00:03:05,800
recommend possibly surgery, possibly radiation, and then they'll get down to chemotherapy. So

00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:16,200
it wouldn't be the first choice simply because there's a lower success rate with chemotherapy,

00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:25,980
with prostate cancer versus like breast cancer. But if I thought the chemotherapy was going to work

00:03:25,980 --> 00:03:33,980
really well for me, would it be wise to start with the lower dose chemotherapy? Yes, it makes sense.

00:03:33,980 --> 00:03:40,220
It makes a lot of sense, but there's negatives to that too. So if you're going to do the lower dose

00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:46,380
chemotherapy, typically you have to do it much more frequently and you have to do many more sessions.

00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:54,620
So while you may not get the abrupt illness jumping right into full dose chemotherapy,

00:03:55,580 --> 00:04:00,860
you can still lose your hair, you can still get really sick, you can still, it just will take

00:04:00,860 --> 00:04:09,820
over a greater length of time. So there's pros and cons to it, so look into both those things.

00:04:10,620 --> 00:04:17,100
And again, if it's not, if chemotherapy isn't going to work for your cancer, low dose chemotherapy

00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:28,060
is not going to work either. You don't have any greater success rate of that.

